{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/qm-pi-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:35:35.952Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f842cf729b33611cb5f55edf4b635ff0057d7faae604699996a4a889bcf81b1e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492.** Source: Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest (5 Oct 2025, teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their bay assignments by text when they checked in. Support patched the text-message routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the next day's 04:00 shift went through without help. A follow-up was set to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419.** Source: Moss's \"North cheat sheet\" (undated, teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The note doesn't say whether it was resolved.\n\nThings to keep out of the deck:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882** are in the Central handoffs digest (2 Jan 2026), but they belong to Pree's dealer account and Marrow Agrisupply, not QFL.\n- **Quarendon Freightways** (one \"r\") is a different company. It's not our customer and uses a competitor's yard software, so don't mix up anything about it with QFL.\n- Moss's other QFL notes have no ticket numbers. The 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest covers call prep for Thea, and the 23 Mar 2026 note covers the renewal.\n\nI only searched Moss's shared notes, so there may be tickets that aren't in these notes. The QFL incident channel, #inc-qfl-sev1, may have more, but you're not a member, so I didn't look there. Dana Okafor, the QFL account owner, would be the person to ask for a full list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
